'''SaintapediaGraph''' is a MediaWiki extension that turns [[Extension:Cargo|Cargo]] tables into interactive [https://mermaid.js.org/ Mermaid] flowcharts. It is maintained for [https://saintapedia.org/ Saintapedia] (org charts and funder → fundee networks) and is usable on any wiki that already runs Cargo.

It does '''not''' require [[Extension:Mermaid]]. Mermaid 10.9.1 is bundled and loaded via ResourceLoader from the wiki origin.

{{note|type=reminder|User-visible messages are '''English only''' (<code>i18n/en.json</code>). Other interface languages fall back to English. There is no translatewiki.net project yet.}}

== Requirements ==

* MediaWiki 1.39 or later
* PHP 8.1 or later
* [[Extension:Cargo]]

== Installation ==

{{ExtensionInstall
|SaintapediaGraph
|download-link=[https://github.com/Saintapedia/SaintapediaGraph/archive/refs/tags/v0.2.4.tar.gz Download v0.2.4]
|registration=required
|localsettingsearly=wfLoadExtension( 'Cargo' );
|custom-steps=
* Optional: import the bundled help page and templates:
<syntaxhighlight lang="bash">
php maintenance/run.php SaintapediaGraph:importPages
</syntaxhighlight>
On MediaWiki 1.39 run <code>php extensions/SaintapediaGraph/maintenance/importPages.php</code> instead. Add <code>--dry-run</code> or <code>--overwrite</code> as needed.
}}

The directory name must be <code>SaintapediaGraph</code> (the ResourceLoader remote path is hardcoded to that name). No <code>update.php</code> run is required.

== Usage ==

Parser functions: <code><nowiki>{{#saintapedia_graph: … }}</nowiki></code> and alias <code><nowiki>{{#cargo_mermaid: … }}</nowiki></code>.

Pick '''one''' mode per diagram:

{| class="wikitable"
! Mode
! Required parameters
|-
| Hierarchy (org chart)
| <code>tables=</code> + <code>parent_field=</code>
|-
| Edge (network)
| <code>tables=</code> + <code>source_field=</code> + <code>target_field=</code>
|-
| Dual-table
| <code>nodes_table=</code> + <code>edges_table=</code> + source/target fields
|}

Dual mode runs two Cargo queries and counts as two expensive parser functions.

=== Org chart ===

<pre>
{{#saintapedia_graph:
tables=Organizations
|fields=_pageName=Name,ParentOrg,Type,Country
|parent_field=ParentOrg
|node_id=Name
|style_by=Type
|subgraph_by=Country
|direction=TD
}}
</pre>

=== Dual-table funding network ===

<pre>
{{#saintapedia_graph:
nodes_table=Organizations
|nodes_fields=_pageName=Name,Type,Country
|edges_table=Grants
|edges_fields=Funder,Recipient,Amount
|edges_where=Year>=2023
|node_id=_pageName
|node_label=Name
|source_field=Funder
|target_field=Recipient
|edge_label=Amount
|style_by=Type
|subgraph_by=Country
|direction=LR
|theme=forest
}}
</pre>

In dual mode, edge endpoints are usually page titles. Prefer <code>node_id=_pageName</code> so they match organization pages.

=== Debug ===

* <code>format=raw</code> — print Mermaid source instead of rendering
* <code>theme=</code> — one of <code>default</code>, <code>base</code>, <code>dark</code>, <code>forest</code>, <code>neutral</code> (anything else falls back to <code>default</code> and warns)
* <code>warn_cycles=yes</code> / <code>break_cycles=yes</code> — report or drop directed back-edges

Full parameter list, template arguments, limits, and troubleshooting: [https://github.com/Saintapedia/SaintapediaGraph/blob/main/docs/Help-Saintapedia_Graph.wikitext Help:Saintapedia Graph (source)] and the [https://github.com/Saintapedia/SaintapediaGraph/blob/main/README.md README].

== Configuration ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Variable
! Default
! Meaning
|-
| <code>$wgSaintapediaGraphDefaultDirection</code>
| <code>TD</code>
| <code>TD</code> / <code>LR</code> / <code>BT</code> / <code>RL</code>
|-
| <code>$wgSaintapediaGraphDefaultLimit</code>
| <code>500</code>
| Default <code>limit=</code> (per Cargo query)
|-
| <code>$wgSaintapediaGraphMaxLimit</code>
| <code>1000</code>
| Hard cap on rows '''per Cargo query'''. Dual-table mode runs two queries, so the total fetched can reach 2× this value.
|-
| <code>$wgSaintapediaGraphClickable</code>
| <code>true</code>
| Nodes link to wiki pages
|-
| <code>$wgSaintapediaGraphDefaultTheme</code>
| <code>default</code>
| Built-in Mermaid theme
|-
| <code>$wgSaintapediaGraphUseStandaloneRenderer</code>
| <code>true</code>
| Interactive render (<code>false</code> = source only)
|-
| <code>$wgSaintapediaGraphWarnCycles</code>
| <code>true</code>
| Warn when directed cycles exist
|-
| <code>$wgSaintapediaGraphBreakCycles</code>
| <code>false</code>
| Drop cycle-closing edges
|-
| <code>$wgSaintapediaGraphStylePalette</code>
| 10 colors
| Fills for <code>style_by</code>
|}

== Security and CSP ==

* Diagram source is stored base64-encoded in a <code>data-mermaid</code> attribute so MediaWiki HTML tidy cannot wrap Mermaid lines in <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;pre&gt;</code>.
* Themes and <code>link_style</code> are allowlisted.
* Node clicks need Mermaid <code>securityLevel: 'loose'</code>. The PHP builder only emits '''same-origin local paths''' from <code>Title::getLocalURL()</code> (no absolute or protocol-relative URLs).
* Scripts are same-origin ResourceLoader only — no CDN. A wiki CSP should allow the wiki origin for <code>script-src</code>. Mermaid 10 also writes some inline SVG styles; a CSP that forbids inline style may leave diagrams unstyled.

== Languages ==

UI strings (errors, warnings, <code>Special:Version</code> description, client render-failure title) are '''English only'''. Additional languages can be added as <code>i18n/&lt;code&gt;.json</code>; there is no translatewiki.net project yet.

